        "integercoordinates": 1,
        "boxes": [
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "gcode",
                    "maxclass": "codebox",
                    "code": "// dingus.toDrumsIn: catches every hit of a trigger / gate signal at the sample, for dingus.toDrums.\n// Max reads signals only once per vector (snapshot~), so a 5 ms trigger can be over before it is read and\n// its velocity reads 0. Here each rise is counted and its level held, so a reader that looks every 2 ms\n// sees every hit (hits closer than that count as one).\n// in1 trigger / gate (level = velocity)\n// out1 one number for one snapshot~: (rises mod 1024) * 256 + velocity (0..127) * 2 + up (1 = the gate is\n//      high); under 2^18, so a 32-bit float carries it exactly. velocity = the peak of the rise's first ms\nHistory up(0);\nHistory rises(0);\nHistory vel(0);\nHistory pk(0);\n\ng = in1;\nif (g > 0 && up == 0) {\n\trises = (rises + 1) % 1024;\n\tvel = g;\n\tpk = floor(samplerate * 0.001);\n\tup = 1;\n} else if (g <= 0 && up > 0) {\n\tup = 0;\n}\n// a trigger that ramps up: its peak over the first ms is the velocity\nif (pk > 0) {\n\tpk = pk - 1;\n\tvel = max(vel, g);\n}\nout1 = rises * 256 + clamp(round(vel * 127), 0, 127) * 2 + up;\n",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
                    "outlettype": [
                        ""
                    ],
                    "patching_rect": [
                        20.0,
                        50.0,
                        620.0,
                        520.0
                    ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "gin1",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "text": "in 1",
                    "numinlets": 0,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
